    ($SATQ$fe4c1c9e$SATQ$, $SATQ$eae9c7b8-873d-4ff8-92bd-dffd8ccec2b8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A mechanical device in a workshop produces items at a constant rate of <math alttext="60"><mn>60</mn>
</math> items per hour. At this rate, how many items will the mechanical device produce in <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> hours?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["180"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["180"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is <math alttext="180"><mn>180</mn>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a mechanical device produces items at a constant rate of <math alttext="60"><mn>60</mn>
</math> items per hour. This rate can be written as <math alttext="StartFraction 60 items Over 1 hour EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represent the number of items the mechanical device will produce in <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> hours at the given rate. It follows that <math alttext="StartFraction 60 items Over 1 hour EndFraction equals StartFraction x items Over 3 hours EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hours</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext="StartFraction 60 Over 1 EndFraction equals StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="60 equals StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction"><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="180 equals x"><mrow>
	<mn>180</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, at the given rate, the mechanical device will produce <math alttext="180"><mn>180</mn>
</math> items in <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> hours.</p>
<p>Alternate approach: It's given that a mechanical device produces items at a constant rate of <math alttext="60"><mn>60</mn>
</math> items per hour. At this rate, the mechanical device will produce <math alttext="left parenthesis StartFraction 60 items Over 1 hour EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 hours right parenthesis"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hours</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="180"><mn>180</mn>
</math> items in <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> hours.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"fe4c1c9e","external_id":"eae9c7b8-873d-4ff8-92bd-dffd8ccec2b8","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"0f199f89-2bc2-4616-af0a-5d9d7e2f53a5","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A mechanical device in a workshop produces items at a constant rate of <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math> items per hour. At this rate, how many items will the mechanical device produce in <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> hours?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["180"],"correct_answer":["180"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a mechanical device produces items at a constant rate of <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math> items per hour. This rate can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 60 items Over 1 hour EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the number of items the mechanical device will produce in <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> hours at the given rate. It follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 60 items Over 1 hour EndFraction equals StartFraction x items Over 3 hours EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hours</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 60 Ove