t parenthesis\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"upper M equals left parenthesis 4 comma 7 plus k right parenthesis\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, side <math alttext=\"upper L upper M\"><mi>L</mi><mi>M</mi></math> is parallel to the <em>y</em>-axis and has a length of <math alttext=\"k plus 2\"><mrow>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"upper L equals left parenthesis 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"upper N equals left parenthesis 6 plus k comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, side <math alttext=\"upper L upper N\"><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></math> is parallel to the <em>x</em>-axis and has a length of <math alttext=\"k plus 2\"><mrow>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, triangle <math alttext=\"upper L upper M upper N\"><mrow>\n<mi>L</mi>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mi>N</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is a right isosceles triangle, where <math alttext=\"angle upper L\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>L</mi></math> has measure <math alttext=\"90 degree\"><mn>90</mn>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper M\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>M</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper N\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> each have measure <math alttext=\"45 degree\"><mn>45</mn>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math>. Of the given choices, only <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 minus t right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math> is equal to <math alttext=\"45 degree\"><mn>45</mn>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math>, so the measure of <math alttext=\"angle upper N\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 minus t right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&deg;</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554986,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"010243e6","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1743430554986,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"c48a5175-a810-4a78-babf-4e18402eb1a3","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"9ac4379c-6eeb-444f-bf7f-cff2538dfd26","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Triangles <math alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>P</mi>\n\t<mi>Q</mi>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper L upper M upper N\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n\t<mi>M</mi>\n\t<mi>N</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> are graphed in the <em>xy</em>-plane. Triangle <math alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>P</mi>\n\t<mi>Q</mi>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> has vertices <math alttext=\"upper P\"><mi>P</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper Q\"><mi>Q</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper R\"><mi>R</mi>\n</math> at <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma 7 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 6 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>, respectively. Triangle <math alttext=\"upper L upper M upper N\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n\t<mi>M</mi>\n\t<mi>N</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> has vertices <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper M\"><mi>M</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper N\"><mi>N</mi>\n</math> at <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma 7 plus k right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 6 plus k comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>, respectively, where <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is a positive constant. If the measure of <math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"t degree\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, what is the measure of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper N\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>?</p>","keys":["926002c1-13ed-4360-b99d-a77b916727fc"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"31dcbf3c-8786-4c1e-95ef-46e0c89f65ce","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 minus left parenthesis t minus k right parenthesis right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"4c93ccb2-bbc7-4252-a7e0-9e7ce610627c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 minus left parenthesis t plus k right parenthesis right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"926002c1-13ed-4360-b99d-a77b916727fc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 minus t right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"ed8f2afc-616d-4b81-8f62-fbbaa5e3f223","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 plus k right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. Since <math alttext=\"upper P equals left parenthesis 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"upper Q equals left parenthesis 4 comma 7 right parenthesis\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, side <math alttext=\"upper P upper Q\"><mrow>\n<mi>P</mi>\n<mi>Q</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is parallel to the <em>y</em>-axis and has a length of <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"upper P equals left parenthesis 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"upper R equals left parenthesis 6 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, side <math alttext=\"upper P upper R\"><mrow>\n<mi>P</mi>\n<mi>R</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is parallel to the <em>x</em>-axis and has a length of <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, triangle <math alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R\"><mrow>\n<mi>P</mi>\n<mi>Q</mi>\n<mi>R</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is a right isosceles triangle, where <math alttext=\"angle upper P\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>P</mi></math> has measure <math alttext=\"90 degree\"><mn>90</mn>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> each have measure <math alttext=\"45 degree\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math>. It follows that if the measure of <math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"t degree\"><mi>t</mi>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math>, then <math alttext=\"t equals 45\"><mrow>\n<mi>t</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>45</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"upper L equals left parenthesis 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"upper M equals left parenthesis 4 comma 7 plus k right parenthesis\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, side <math alttext=\"upper L upper M\"><mi>L</mi><mi>M</mi></math> is parallel to the <em>y</em>-axis and has a length of <math alttext=\"k plus 2\"><mrow>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"upper L equals left parenthesis 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"upper N equals left parenthesis 6 plus k comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, side <math alttext=\"upper L upper N\"><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></math> is parallel to the <em>x</em>-axis and has a length of <math alttext=\"k plus 2\"><mrow>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, triangle <math alttext=\"upper L upper M upper N\"><mrow>\n<mi>L</mi>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mi>N</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is a right isosceles triangle, where <math alttext=\"angle upper L\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>L</mi></math> has measure <math alttext=\"90 degree\"><mn>90</mn>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper M\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>M</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper N\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> each have measure <math alttext=\"45 degree\"><mn>45</mn>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math>. Of the given choices, only <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 minus t right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math> is equal to <math alttext=\"45 degree\"><mn>45</mn>\n<mo>&deg;</mo></math>, so the measure of <math alttext=\"angle upper N\"><mo>&ang;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 90 minus t right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&deg;</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"c48a5175-a810-4a78-babf-4e18402eb1a3","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1743430554986,"updateDate":1743430554986}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554986, 1743430554986),
