<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the length of <math alttext="line segment upper Y upper Z"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, not <math alttext="line segment upper X upper Y"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"055aafe7","external_id":"e2fa4379-f216-4286-8c00-6098b985ceea","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"282bf10d-8dc8-4041-bf86-352674ff095d","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> correspond to <math alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper Z\"><mi>Z</mi>\n</math>, respectively. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper A upper B\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> and the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"850\"><mn>850</mn>\n</math>. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper Y upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math>. What is the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f316b5ac-8bc2-466c-9d8e-78bdf3f50e87","content":"<p><math alttext=\"204\"><mn>204</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cd80f4f5-ed45-4ea1-ab4f-838db24f0ce3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"182\"><mn>182</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"043aaa10-6bdc-42c7-9e09-2ddd5f563d14","content":"<p><math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4e416e9b-503f-45ab-9d18-1e23b0a9771b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["4e416e9b-503f-45ab-9d18-1e23b0a9771b"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n<mi>X</mi>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> correspond to <math alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper Z\"><mi>Z</mi>\n</math>, respectively. It follows that side <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> corresponds to side <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y\"><mrow>\n<mi>X</mi>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and side <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> corresponds to side <math alttext=\"upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since the lengths of corresponding sides in similar triangles are proportional, it follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction upper X upper Y Over upper A upper B EndFraction equals StartFraction upper Y upper Z Over upper B upper C EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"850\"><mn>850</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> in this equation yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction upper X upper Y Over 170 EndFraction equals StartFraction 60 Over 850 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mn>170</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>850</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y equals 12\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>X</mi>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>12</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper Y upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, not <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554987,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"055aafe7","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1743430554987,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"e2fa4379-f216-4286-8c00-6098b985ceea","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"282bf10d-8dc8-4041-bf86-352674ff095d","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> correspond to <math alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper Z\"><mi>Z</mi>\n</math>, respectively. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper A upper B\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> and the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"850\"><mn>850</mn>\n</math>. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper Y upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math>. What is the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>?</p>","keys":["4e416e9b-503f-45ab-9d18-1e23b0a9771b"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"f316b5ac-8bc2-466c-9d8e-78bdf3f50e87","content":"<p><math alttext=\"204\"><mn>204</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cd80f4f5-ed45-4ea1-ab4f-838db24f0ce3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"182\"><mn>182</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"043aaa10-6bdc-42c7-9e09-2ddd5f563d14","content":"<p><math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4e416e9b-503f-45ab-9d18-1e23b0a9771b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n<mi>X</mi>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> correspond to <math alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper Z\"><mi>Z</mi>\n</math>, respectively. It follows that side <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> corresponds to side <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y\"><mrow>\n<mi>X</mi>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and side <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> corresponds to side <math alttext=\"upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since the lengths of corresponding sides in similar triangles are proportional, it follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction upper X upper Y Over upper A upper B EndFraction equals StartFraction upper Y upper Z Over upper B upper C EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"850\"><mn>850</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> in this equation yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction upper X upper Y Over 170 EndFraction equals StartFraction 60 Over 850 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mn>170</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>850</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y equals 12\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>X</mi>\n<mi>Y</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>12</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper Y upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, not <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>.</p>","externalid":"e2fa4379-f216-4286-8c00-6098b985ceea","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1743430554987,"updateDate":1743430554987}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554987, 1743430554987),
