</math> is the area of the base and <math alttext="h"><mi>h</mi>
</math> is the height of the prism. Therefore, <math alttext="216 equals upper B h"><mn>216</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>h</mi></math>. It's also given that the triangular prism has a height of <math alttext="8 cm"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. Therefore, <math alttext="h equals 8"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
