</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"08b7a3f5","external_id":"357b0938-dcf1-4984-934a-7d55d036717a","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"d6c9e931-525b-4fc3-a63e-e804d97672ac","uId":"9b43475c-f945-4a45-8831-bf99ef82f097","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>A triangular prism has a height of <math alttext=\"8 centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math> and a volume of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"216 cm cubed\"><mrow><mn>216</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. What is the area, <math alttext=\"in cm squared\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">2</mi></msup></math>, of the base of the prism? (The volume of a triangular prism is equal to <math alttext=\"upper B h\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>h</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math> is the area of the base and <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> is the height of the prism.)</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["27"],"correct_answer":["27"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>. It's given that a triangular prism has a volume of <math alttext=\"216 cubic centimeters left parenthesis cm cubed right parenthesis\"><mn>216</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cubic&#160;centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mfenced></math> and the volume of a triangular prism is equal to <math alttext=\"upper B h\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>h</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper B\"><